WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.793
♪♪

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:04.254
Rebecca Ferguson:
As an actor, to walk onto a set

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:09.968
Rebecca Ferguson:
where you have depth and height
and shape and everything is authentic,

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.722
it just creates realism for us
to play around it.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.229
♪♪

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:22.314
Hugh Howey:
The Silo is incredibly
cinematic.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.275
It’s a new world told in a
completely new way.

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:30.739
This is as big as any feature
film, the number of sets we have
is seventy plus.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.075
Morten Tyldum:
When we designed the Silo,

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.411
we decided to make all the
building blocks circular.

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:40.999
Morten Tyldum:
All the alleyways, the
stairways, everything has this round development to it.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.502
The sets are incredibly moving.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:46.380
Graham Yost:
They are the cathedral of the
whole story.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.299
Rashida Jones:
Everything is magical.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:54.596
It’s so detailed, it’s so
beautiful, the world is so well
realized.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:55.389
(Cheering)

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:58.517
Gavin Bocquet:
Life in the Silo replicates a
lot of things we’re used to in our world,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.186
Gavin Bocquet:
from living spaces to factories to
farms.

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.315
It’s a complete world built a
mile down into the earth.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:10.946
♪♪

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:14.783
Hugh Howey:
The experience of watching the
world of the Silo come to life

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:15.909
absolutely blew me away. 

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.247
Hugh Howey:
The scope of the Silo was even
bigger and more awe-inspiring than I imagined.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.333
Rebecca Ferguson:
Everything is used.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:24.543
Rebecca Ferguson:
Everything is recycled.

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:28.380
Rebecca Ferguson:
Whether they are phones or
watches or a little PEZ dispenser.

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.134
It’s so detailed, it’s so
stunning.

00:01:32.134 --> 00:01:34.469
♪♪

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:37.389
It is just a gift to be able to
get lost in this

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:41.476
world in a way that feels
completely real.

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:43.729
♪♪

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:45.397
Morten Tyldum:
Creating the world of the Silo,

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:47.858
we wanted it to feel like
nothing you’ve seen anywhere
else.

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:51.403
♪♪

